  "source_decisions": [
    "The saved-character getter and the inventory accessor return named records. The accessor takes the actual inventory receiver at the start of the record.",
    "The two saved-player callers share a constructor declaration with a 16-bit slot argument. The C++ member-call form changed instruction order in two exact retail functions. The shared typed declaration matches both callers and preserves slot truncation.",
    "The public factory and character-state methods take TPlyCharData pointers. The packet and legacy scratch buffers retain their byte layouts.",
    "The older inventory sort buffer uses native entry records and exact runtime allocation calls. The older new-array code and offset-named owner fields remain part of the historical source comparison."
  ]
